CONTEXT=urn:cts:compnov:bible.genesis.vulgate:42.13.t0-urn:cts:compnov:bible.genesis.vulgate:42.13.t30
REASONING=The sentence frames a quoted reply. "At illi" supplies the subject ("illi") of the framing verb "inquiunt", which is the independent verb; the quoted words contain three finite verbs ("sumus", "est", "est"), each of syntactic type 'direct quote' related to "inquiunt". Within the quote: "Duodecim servi tui fratres sumus" — "Duodecim" is a spelled-out number word (hence lexical) modifying "servi" adjectivally; "servi tui" is the subject of "sumus", "fratres" its predicate. "filii viri unius in terra Chanaan" stands in apposition to "servi", with "viri" as a genitive depending on "filii", "unius" adjectival to "viri", and the prepositional phrase "in terra Chanaan" attributive to "viri" ("Chanaan" a genitive with "terra"). "minimus cum patre nostro est": "minimus" (substantival adjective) is subject, "cum" adverbial to "est" with "patre" as its object and "nostro" adjectival. "alius non est super": "alius" subject, "non" and "super" adverbial to "est". Both of these "est" forms express existence/location, so intransitive; "sumus" with predicate "fratres" is a linking verb. "At" is a coordinating conjunction opening the sentence with no preceding verb to pair with, so only relatedtoken1 -> "inquiunt".

